WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.098 --> 00:00:00.994
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:00.994 --> 00:00:02.512
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.512 --> 00:00:04.438
My one word is believe and I believe

00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:05.907
that entrepreneurs will solve all

00:00:05.907 --> 00:00:07.784
of the major problems of the world.

00:00:07.784 --> 00:00:11.412
So today's message is create your own art.

00:00:11.412 --> 00:00:12.798
Over to you Bruce Lee.

00:00:12.798 --> 00:00:15.281
(rooster crows)

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.918
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.918 --> 00:00:20.703
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:20.703 --> 00:00:24.203
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:28.720
- [Narrator] In case you
have missed the recent news,

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.561
Jeet Kune Do, of which I am the founder,

00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:35.059
has been elected and accepted into

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:38.309
the black belt hall of fame in America.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:43.377
This marks the first
time a recently developed

00:00:43.377 --> 00:00:46.960
form of martial art is
nationally accepted.

00:00:48.751 --> 00:00:51.953
No, Jeet Kune Do is not thousands

00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:54.667
or even hundreds of years old.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.750
It started in around 1965

00:00:59.246 --> 00:01:03.413
by a dedicated and intensified
man called Bruce Lee.

00:01:04.953 --> 00:01:07.619
My martial art is something that

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:11.040
no serious martial artist can ignore.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.518
- If you want to reach
your true potential,

00:01:12.518 --> 00:01:14.550
then you need to create your own art.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.252
At the beginning, you can model success.

00:01:16.252 --> 00:01:17.860
You can copy what other people are doing.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.231
You can learn from others
and you can apply it

00:01:20.231 --> 00:01:23.478
to build whatever product
or service you have up

00:01:23.478 --> 00:01:25.628
but at some point you have to say,

00:01:25.628 --> 00:01:27.293
this is where I deviate.

00:01:27.293 --> 00:01:28.949
This is where I become me.

00:01:28.949 --> 00:01:30.463
This is where I branch off

00:01:30.463 --> 00:01:32.808
and differentiate myself
from everybody else.

00:01:32.808 --> 00:01:34.984
At the beginning, it's
great to model success.

00:01:34.984 --> 00:01:36.266
When I was building up my Youtube channel,

00:01:36.266 --> 00:01:38.384
I had a media coach through my agent,

00:01:38.384 --> 00:01:41.812
and my agent and her taught me every week

00:01:41.812 --> 00:01:44.010
and gave me advice on how to get better.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.464
I would copy and paste what they gave me

00:01:46.464 --> 00:01:49.155
and it would actually never
quite work out perfectly.

00:01:49.155 --> 00:01:50.032
I always had to tweak it.

00:01:50.032 --> 00:01:53.133
I always had to change
it to make it fit me.

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:55.706
When I'm modeling Steve
Jobs or Opera Winfrey

00:01:55.706 --> 00:01:57.741
or whoever it is, Howard Shultz,

00:01:57.741 --> 00:01:59.982
I can't do it exactly like they did it.

00:01:59.982 --> 00:02:04.013
Got to take it and tweak
it and make it fit for me.

00:02:04.013 --> 00:02:06.207
That's what you have
to do in your business.

00:02:06.207 --> 00:02:07.922
You got to find what is the unique twist

00:02:07.922 --> 00:02:10.132
that you bring that,
yes, you can copy others

00:02:10.132 --> 00:02:12.625
and model others but
at the end of the day,

00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:15.720
you're switching it up and just
a little bit, little tweak.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.516
That is unique and special.

00:02:17.516 --> 00:02:18.830
That's why I don't care about people

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.312
who copy my Youtube channel.

00:02:20.312 --> 00:02:23.007
People send me emails
all the time and comments

00:02:23.007 --> 00:02:24.919
like this person copied your video

00:02:24.919 --> 00:02:26.687
or is doing exactly like you're doing.

00:02:26.687 --> 00:02:30.104
The best they're ever going to
be is an Evan Carmichael junior.

00:02:30.104 --> 00:02:33.202
So I either spend my time
worrying about those guys

00:02:33.202 --> 00:02:35.731
or I spend my time
building something better.

00:02:35.731 --> 00:02:37.811
Like if all you're doing
is copying somebody else,

00:02:37.811 --> 00:02:40.619
you're only going to be
a junior version of them.

00:02:40.619 --> 00:02:42.647
So I don't care about those people

00:02:42.647 --> 00:02:43.791
'cause they can't catch up.

00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:46.178
They're always playing from behind.

00:02:46.178 --> 00:02:49.316
I want to focus on
building my future forward.

00:02:49.316 --> 00:02:50.849
I look at Lily as an example,

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:54.437
who's in the Unlocking Lily
series on my channel right now.

00:02:54.437 --> 00:02:56.407
I hired her away for a full-time job.

00:02:56.407 --> 00:02:57.902
She wanted to be a professional speaker

00:02:57.902 --> 00:03:00.562
and so I'm coaching and
training her on how to do it.

00:03:00.562 --> 00:03:02.443
I'm following and documenting the journey.

00:03:02.443 --> 00:03:05.543
Hopefully you guys are
learning along in the process.

00:03:05.543 --> 00:03:08.696
At the start, she's taking parallel paths.

00:03:08.696 --> 00:03:11.209
She doesn't know her message yet.

00:03:11.209 --> 00:03:12.114
She hasn't figured it out.

00:03:12.114 --> 00:03:14.703
She's researching, she's watching videos,

00:03:14.703 --> 00:03:17.181
she's reading, she's
trying to formulate it.

00:03:17.181 --> 00:03:21.050
At the same time, I want her out speaking

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.735
to get the practice,
to get the experience,

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:25.605
to get the knowledge, to get the reps in.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:29.772
So what she's doing at the
start is teaching Your One Word.

00:03:30.613 --> 00:03:32.409
She's running workshops,
she's doing coaching,

00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:34.536
she's doing one-on-one,
she's doing seminars,

00:03:34.536 --> 00:03:37.378
she's doing college, she's
doing Hangouts, Skype sessions.

00:03:37.378 --> 00:03:40.095
She's helping people around Your One Word.

00:03:40.095 --> 00:03:40.928
And it's great.

00:03:40.928 --> 00:03:42.581
She does bring her own little twist to it

00:03:42.581 --> 00:03:44.931
but at the end of the day,
this is my philosophy.

00:03:44.931 --> 00:03:48.799
Lily will not stay doing
Your One Word forever.

00:03:48.799 --> 00:03:52.176
Otherwise, she won't be
able to unleash her art.

00:03:52.176 --> 00:03:54.482
So she's copying and
modeling what I've done

00:03:54.482 --> 00:03:57.299
to propel her path forward
while at the same time

00:03:57.299 --> 00:03:59.633
figuring her message
because at some point,

00:03:59.633 --> 00:04:01.518
her thing is going to take over.

00:04:01.518 --> 00:04:03.219
That's what you need to do as well.

00:04:03.219 --> 00:04:04.302
It's okay to copy somebody.

00:04:04.302 --> 00:04:07.313
It's okay to model somebody
who's done a lot more than you.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.252
But at some point, you need to break off

00:04:09.252 --> 00:04:11.573
and say here's where I'm different.

00:04:11.573 --> 00:04:12.764
Here's where I'm special.

00:04:12.764 --> 00:04:15.597
Here's a little magic
dust that only I can bring

00:04:15.597 --> 00:04:17.770
to this new way of doing something.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.234
When you do that and
you create your own art,

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:22.605
that's when you will
reach your true potential.

00:04:22.605 --> 00:04:24.276
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious

00:04:24.276 --> 00:04:26.831
what is the unique thing that you bring

00:04:26.831 --> 00:04:29.900
that's different from everybody
else in your industry?

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.317
What is your unique art?

00:04:31.317 --> 00:04:32.422
I'm really curious.

00:04:32.422 --> 00:04:33.844
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:04:33.844 --> 00:04:34.942
I want to find out.

00:04:34.942 --> 00:04:36.705
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Joel Wasserman.

00:04:36.705 --> 00:04:38.259
Joel, thank you so much for picking up

00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:40.166
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:41.757
Really, really, really
means a lot to me man

00:04:41.757 --> 00:04:43.490
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:44.952
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:44.952 --> 00:04:46.167
I believe in you.

00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:48.065
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:48.065 --> 00:04:50.124
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:50.124 --> 00:04:51.676
I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:51.676 --> 00:04:54.161
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:54.161 --> 00:04:56.928
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:56.928 --> 00:05:00.511
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:11.139
- I was drawn into a plumbing trade.

00:05:11.139 --> 00:05:12.191
I didn't give a (swear
bleeps) about plumbing,

00:05:12.191 --> 00:05:14.247
didn't know anything about plumbing.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.612
I just went on that side because culture

00:05:16.612 --> 00:05:19.147
told me that that's what I have to do.

00:05:19.147 --> 00:05:21.711
I done it for a while and then I realized

00:05:21.711 --> 00:05:23.582
this is not what I want to do.

00:05:23.582 --> 00:05:24.655
If this is not what I want to do

00:05:24.655 --> 00:05:26.579
then what the (swear
bleeps) am I doing it for?

00:05:26.579 --> 00:05:29.246
I walked out 18 months in maybe.

00:05:30.177 --> 00:05:32.189
- There was a concern there for us,

00:05:32.189 --> 00:05:33.272
for his mother and father.

00:05:33.272 --> 00:05:34.407
We didn't know what he was going to do

00:05:34.407 --> 00:05:36.240
to be honest with you.

00:05:38.741 --> 00:05:40.299
Early on, obviously I
didn't know what it was.

00:05:40.299 --> 00:05:43.878
I couldn't look to my mother and say, hey.

00:05:43.878 --> 00:05:46.646
This Irishman, Donnie, I'm
going to follow in his footsteps

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:47.931
because there was no footsteps.

00:05:47.931 --> 00:05:52.226
I had to create my own
footsteps and follow them.

00:05:52.226 --> 00:05:54.168
They were a little unsure at first

00:05:54.168 --> 00:05:57.098
but they supported me and
they knew I would do it

00:05:57.098 --> 00:05:59.481
if I said I'd do it, I'd do it, so.

00:05:59.481 --> 00:06:03.416
- The question is, are we rock and roll?

00:06:03.416 --> 00:06:06.638
(audience cheers and claps)

00:06:06.638 --> 00:06:09.235
And I say you're goddamn
right, we rock and roll.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:12.652
(audience cheers louder)

00:06:18.012 --> 00:06:21.345
See, rock and roll is not an instrument.

00:06:22.438 --> 00:06:25.533
Rock and roll is not
even a style of music.

00:06:25.533 --> 00:06:28.085
Rock and roll is a spirit.

00:06:28.085 --> 00:06:29.252
It's a spirit.

00:06:31.343 --> 00:06:33.723
It's been going since the blues,

00:06:33.723 --> 00:06:36.890
jazz, bebop, soul, R&amp;B, rock and roll,

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:43.007
heavy metal, punk rock, and yes, hip hop.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:46.900
(audience applauds)

00:06:52.692 --> 00:06:56.344
What connects us all is that spirit.

00:06:56.344 --> 00:06:58.101
That's what connects us all.

00:06:58.101 --> 00:06:59.834
That spirit.

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:02.417
Rock and roll is not conforming

00:07:04.304 --> 00:07:07.137
to the people who came before you,

00:07:08.181 --> 00:07:12.989
but creating your own
path in music and in life.

00:07:12.989 --> 00:07:16.156
That is rock and roll, and that is us.

00:07:25.965 --> 00:07:29.167
Rock and roll is not conforming.

00:07:29.167 --> 00:07:31.842
Rock and roll is outside the box.

00:07:31.842 --> 00:07:34.561
Rock and roll is N.W.A.

00:07:34.561 --> 00:07:38.299
I want to thank everybody
who helped induct us

00:07:38.299 --> 00:07:40.905
into the rock and roll hall of fame.

00:07:40.905 --> 00:07:43.069
I just want to tell the world

00:07:43.069 --> 00:07:44.652
damn that was dope.

00:07:45.521 --> 00:07:48.009
Thank you, we out of here.

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:49.681
- I tell all young people,

00:07:49.681 --> 00:07:51.119
I say to you right now.

00:07:51.119 --> 00:07:54.175
Stop looking for employment.

00:07:54.175 --> 00:07:56.387
Why don't you position
yourself differently

00:07:56.387 --> 00:07:58.387
and look for deployment?

00:07:59.421 --> 00:08:01.179
To employees, to be employed means that

00:08:01.179 --> 00:08:04.274
somebody else is benefiting
from your energy.

00:08:04.274 --> 00:08:07.069
To deploy means, to deploy yourself

00:08:07.069 --> 00:08:10.676
means that you are using your
own energy to be productive.

00:08:10.676 --> 00:08:13.447
So instead of waiting for
somebody to give you a job,

00:08:13.447 --> 00:08:15.607
create your own work.

00:08:15.607 --> 00:08:16.911
That's why I tell, 'cause it's different

00:08:16.911 --> 00:08:19.574
between your work and your job.

00:08:19.574 --> 00:08:22.680
Your job is what they train you to do.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:25.991
Your work is what you were born to do.

00:08:25.991 --> 00:08:27.813
Your job is your skill

00:08:27.813 --> 00:08:29.764
which they can fire you from at anytime.

00:08:29.764 --> 00:08:31.328
But your work is your gift.

00:08:31.328 --> 00:08:33.352
No one can take that from you.

00:08:33.352 --> 00:08:37.773
Your job is for you to get
compensation for activity.

00:08:37.773 --> 00:08:39.996
Your work is when you get fulfillment

00:08:39.996 --> 00:08:41.935
'cause you love it so much.

00:08:41.935 --> 00:08:43.994
Your job, you can retire from.

00:08:43.994 --> 00:08:45.075
Your work, you can never retire

00:08:45.075 --> 00:08:47.433
from your work 'cause your work is you.

00:08:47.433 --> 00:08:50.033
So when a person discovers their work,

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:51.670
they no longer need a job

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.647
'cause their work makes them productive.

00:08:53.647 --> 00:08:55.604
So the young people in this country

00:08:55.604 --> 00:08:57.832
who are full of talent, full of gifts

00:08:57.832 --> 00:09:00.082
and I want to say this too.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:04.050
Every problem in life is a business.

00:09:05.132 --> 00:09:08.769
All business is simply
someone solving a problem.

00:09:08.769 --> 00:09:11.232
So the more problems that I encounter,

00:09:11.232 --> 00:09:14.597
the more businesses available
for young people to begin.

00:09:14.597 --> 00:09:16.716
This is what I think we're lacking.

00:09:16.716 --> 00:09:19.312
We are trained to get a job.

00:09:19.312 --> 00:09:22.307
We are trained to start a business.

00:09:22.307 --> 00:09:25.608
We are trained to let
other people employ us

00:09:25.608 --> 00:09:27.654
not trained to deploy ourselves.

